<h3 id='options-order-book'>Order Book</h3>

`GET /v1/market/orderBook`

Get the order book details for the provided symbol.

<table>
   <thead>
      <tr>
         <th>Parameter</th>
         <th>Type</th>
         <th>Required</th>
         <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
   </thead>
   <tbody>
      <tr>
         <td>symbol</td>
         <td>string</td>
         <td>Yes</td>
         <td>The unique option contract symbol, e.g., "BTC-7JUL25-108000-C-USDT". This encodes the base asset, expiration date, strike price, option type (Call/Put), and quote asset.</td>
      </tr>
   </tbody>
</table>

### Response

The response parameters are as follows:

```json
// Response
{
  "symbol": "BTC-7AUG25-117500-P-USDT",
  "bids": [
    [
      "3975",
      "0.02"
    ]
  ],
  "asks": [
    [
      "3980",
      "0.02"
    ]
  ]
}
```

<table>
   <thead>
      <tr>
         <th>Parameter</th>
         <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
   </thead>
   <tbody>
      <tr>
         <td><strong>symbol</strong></td>
         <td>The unique option contract symbol, e.g., "BTC-7AUG25-117500-P-USDT". It encodes the base asset, expiration date, strike price, option type (Call/Put), and quote asset.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
         <td><strong>bids</strong></td>
         <td>List of bid orders. Each item is an array with price and quantity strings, e.g., ["3975", "0.02"].</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
         <td><strong>asks</strong></td>
         <td>List of ask orders. Each item is an array with price and quantity strings, e.g., ["3980", "0.02"].</td>
      </tr>
   </tbody>
</table>

